<ArchivePost
  title="WordPress Publishing Error"
  date="3 December 2019"
  tags="WordPress"
  description="Tracing an invalid JSON response in WordPress back to a local HTTPS mismatch."
  canonicalPath="/pensieve/wordpress-publish-error/"
>
  <h2>Problem</h2>
  <p>
    While working on a local WordPress project, I could not update or publish a post from the
    admin. WordPress sometimes returned the more useful message:
  </p>
  <blockquote>Publishing failed. Error message: The response is not a valid JSON response.</blockquote>

  <h2>Solution</h2>
  <p>
    The JSON message initially suggested a Gutenberg or ACF problem. The actual issue was a
    protocol mismatch: the admin was loaded over HTTPS while the local site used HTTP, producing
    a CORS error.
  </p>
  <p>Opening the local WordPress admin over HTTP allowed posts to publish normally.</p>
</ArchivePost>
